IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `cidra-types`
IMPORT `cidra-misrepresentation`
IMPORT `cidra-remedies`
IMPORT `cidra-goal`

-- Consumer Insurance (Disclosure and Representations) Act 2012 (UK) —
-- INDEPENDENT tests. Expected values were fixed in independent-expectations.md
-- from the Act alone, before the encoding was read. A failing assertion is a
-- finding; no expected value has been changed to match the code.
-- Scenario ids (A1, Q5, R14 ...) refer to independent-expectations.md.

§ `Independent tests`

-- Builders (positional records, declared field order).

GIVEN ind IS A BOOLEAN, purp IS A BOOLEAN, ins IS A BOOLEAN, after IS A BOOLEAN, life IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Contract facts`
`a contract` ind purp ins after life MEANS
    `Contract facts` OF ind, purp, ins, after, life

GIVEN made IS A BOOLEAN, care IS A BOOLEAN, dishonest IS A BOOLEAN,
      ku IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN, rcu IS A BOOLEAN, kr IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN, rcr IS A BOOLEAN, clear IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Misrepresentation facts`
`a misrep` made care dishonest ku rcu kr rcr clear MEANS
    `Misrepresentation facts` OF made, care, dishonest, ku, rcu, kr, rcr, clear

GIVEN d IS A BOOLEAN, h IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `What the insurer would have done`
`entered with` d h MEANS
    `the contract, on these terms` OF d, h

GIVEN charged IS A NUMBER, paid IS A NUMBER, unfair IS A NUMBER, actual IS A NUMBER, diff IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Money facts`
`money` charged paid unfair actual diff MEANS
    `Money facts` OF charged, paid, unfair, actual, diff

-- Base facts.
consumerK MEANS `a contract` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE
lifeK MEANS `a contract` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE

-- No reasonable care; nothing shown about state of mind; no presumption facts:
-- careless if qualifying (C7).
carelessM MEANS `a misrep` TRUE FALSE FALSE NOTHING FALSE NOTHING FALSE FALSE
-- Knew untrue and knew relevant (C1).
deliberateM MEANS `a misrep` TRUE FALSE FALSE (JUST TRUE) FALSE (JUST TRUE) FALSE FALSE
-- Reasonable care, honest.
carefulM MEANS `a misrep` TRUE TRUE FALSE NOTHING FALSE NOTHING FALSE FALSE

baseX MEANS `money` 300 300 0 10000 10000

higher400 MEANS `entered with` FALSE 400

§§ `Goal 1 — does the Act apply (ss 1, 12(4))`

-- A1 base
#ASSERT `the Act applies to` consumerK
-- A2 mainly private: the purpose flag covers "wholly or mainly"
#ASSERT `the Act applies to` (`a contract` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE)
-- A3 / A13 mainly business
#ASSERT NOT (`the Act applies to` (`a contract` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE))
-- A4 company
#ASSERT NOT (`the Act applies to` (`a contract` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE))
-- A5 / A6 not party by way of an insurance business
#ASSERT NOT (`the Act applies to` (`a contract` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE))
-- A8 / A11 / A12 entered before commencement (the encoding takes this as a
-- boolean; dates are not computed — see report)
#ASSERT NOT (`the Act applies to` (`a contract` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE))
-- life insurance is still consumer insurance
#ASSERT `the Act applies to` lifeK

§§ `Goal 2 — qualifying misrepresentation (ss 2(2), 3(5), 4(1))`

-- Q1 no care, would not have entered at all
#ASSERT `is a qualifying misrepresentation` carelessM `given` `no contract on any terms` `and` baseX
-- Q2 reasonable care, honest
#ASSERT NOT (`is a qualifying misrepresentation` carefulM `given` `no contract on any terms` `and` baseX)
-- Q3 reasonable care found, but dishonest: s 3(5)
#ASSERT `is a qualifying misrepresentation` (`a misrep` TRUE TRUE TRUE (JUST TRUE) FALSE (JUST TRUE) FALSE FALSE) `given` `no contract on any terms` `and` baseX
-- Q4 same terms, same premium
#ASSERT NOT (`is a qualifying misrepresentation` carelessM `given` `the same contract on the same terms` `and` baseX)
-- Q5 higher premium only
#ASSERT `is a qualifying misrepresentation` carelessM `given` higher400 `and` baseX
-- Q6 exclusion, same premium
#ASSERT `is a qualifying misrepresentation` carelessM `given` (`entered with` TRUE 300) `and` baseX
-- Q7 exclusion and higher premium
#ASSERT `is a qualifying misrepresentation` carelessM `given` (`entered with` TRUE 400) `and` baseX
-- Q8 reasonable care, higher premium
#ASSERT NOT (`is a qualifying misrepresentation` carefulM `given` higher400 `and` baseX)
-- Q9 "higher" premium equal to the premium charged
#ASSERT NOT (`is a qualifying misrepresentation` carelessM `given` (`entered with` FALSE 300) `and` baseX)
-- Q10 dishonest, reasonable care found, higher premium only
#ASSERT `is a qualifying misrepresentation` (`a misrep` TRUE TRUE TRUE (JUST TRUE) FALSE (JUST TRUE) FALSE FALSE) `given` higher400 `and` baseX
-- no misrepresentation made at all
#ASSERT NOT (`is a qualifying misrepresentation` (`a misrep` FALSE FALSE FALSE NOTHING FALSE NOTHING FALSE FALSE) `given` `no contract on any terms` `and` baseX)

§§ `Goal 2 — class (s 5)`

-- C1 knew untrue, knew relevant
#ASSERT `the class of` deliberateM EQUALS `deliberate or reckless`
-- C2 / C3 / C4 "did not care" (folded into the same fields)
#ASSERT `the class of` (`a misrep` TRUE FALSE FALSE (JUST TRUE) FALSE (JUST TRUE) FALSE TRUE) EQUALS `deliberate or reckless`
-- C5 knew untrue; shown not to know relevance; no clear question
#ASSERT `the class of` (`a misrep` TRUE FALSE FALSE (JUST TRUE) FALSE (JUST FALSE) FALSE FALSE) EQUALS `careless`
-- C6 honestly believed true; knew relevant
#ASSERT `the class of` (`a misrep` TRUE FALSE FALSE (JUST FALSE) FALSE (JUST TRUE) FALSE FALSE) EQUALS `careless`
-- C7 nothing shown; no presumption facts: burden on insurer, s 5(4)
#ASSERT `the class of` carelessM EQUALS `careless`
-- C8 knew untrue; relevance not shown; clear and specific question: s 5(5)(b)
#ASSERT `the class of` (`a misrep` TRUE FALSE FALSE (JUST TRUE) FALSE NOTHING FALSE TRUE) EQUALS `deliberate or reckless`
-- C9 as C8, contrary shown
#ASSERT `the class of` (`a misrep` TRUE FALSE FALSE (JUST TRUE) FALSE (JUST FALSE) FALSE TRUE) EQUALS `careless`
-- C10 knowledge not shown; reasonable consumer would have known both: s 5(5)(a)
#ASSERT `the class of` (`a misrep` TRUE FALSE FALSE NOTHING TRUE NOTHING TRUE FALSE) EQUALS `deliberate or reckless`
-- C11 as C10, contrary shown on both
#ASSERT `the class of` (`a misrep` TRUE FALSE FALSE (JUST FALSE) TRUE (JUST FALSE) TRUE FALSE) EQUALS `careless`
-- C11b as C10, contrary shown on untruth only
#ASSERT `the class of` (`a misrep` TRUE FALSE FALSE (JUST FALSE) TRUE NOTHING TRUE TRUE) EQUALS `careless`
-- C12 knew untrue; relevance not shown; no clear question; reasonable consumer would not have known relevance
#ASSERT `the class of` (`a misrep` TRUE FALSE FALSE (JUST TRUE) FALSE NOTHING FALSE FALSE) EQUALS `careless`
-- presumption (a) on untruth plus presumption (b) on relevance
#ASSERT `the class of` (`a misrep` TRUE FALSE FALSE NOTHING TRUE NOTHING FALSE TRUE) EQUALS `deliberate or reckless`

§§ `Goal 3 — remedies, para 2 (deliberate or reckless)`

r1 MEANS `the insurer's remedy for` consumerK `and` deliberateM `given` `no contract on any terms` `and` (`money` 1200 1200 0 10000 10000)
-- R1
#ASSERT r1's `may avoid the contract and refuse all claims`
#ASSERT r1's `amount payable on the claim` EQUALS 0
#ASSERT r1's `premiums to return` EQUALS 0
-- para 9 does not apply to deliberate or reckless (F9)
#ASSERT NOT (r1's `may terminate by reasonable notice`)
#ASSERT NOT (r1's `may give notice of its rights for the future`)

r2 MEANS `the insurer's remedy for` consumerK `and` deliberateM `given` higher400 `and` (`money` 300 1200 300 10000 10000)
-- R2: para 2 applies whatever the insurer would have done
#ASSERT r2's `may avoid the contract and refuse all claims`
#ASSERT r2's `premiums to return` EQUALS 300
#ASSERT r2's `amount payable on the claim` EQUALS 0

r3 MEANS `the insurer's remedy for` consumerK `and` deliberateM `given` higher400 `and` (`money` 300 1200 1200 10000 10000)
-- R3
#ASSERT r3's `premiums to return` EQUALS 1200

§§ `Goal 3 — remedies, para 5 (careless, not on any terms)`

r4 MEANS `the insurer's remedy for` consumerK `and` carelessM `given` `no contract on any terms` `and` (`money` 1200 1200 0 10000 10000)
-- R4
#ASSERT r4's `may avoid the contract and refuse all claims`
#ASSERT r4's `amount payable on the claim` EQUALS 0
#ASSERT r4's `premiums to return` EQUALS 1200
-- F8: para 9(4) not triggered by para 5
#ASSERT NOT (r4's `may give notice of its rights for the future`)
#ASSERT NOT (r4's `may terminate by reasonable notice`)

r5 MEANS `the insurer's remedy for` consumerK `and` carelessM `given` `no contract on any terms` `and` (`money` 1200 1200 300 10000 10000)
-- R5: "unfair" figure irrelevant to para 5
#ASSERT r5's `premiums to return` EQUALS 1200

§§ `Goal 3 — remedies, para 6 (different terms)`

r6 MEANS `the insurer's remedy for` consumerK `and` carelessM `given` (`entered with` TRUE 300) `and` (`money` 300 300 0 10000 0)
-- R6
#ASSERT r6's `contract treated as on the different terms`
#ASSERT r6's `amount payable on the claim` EQUALS 0
#ASSERT NOT (r6's `may avoid the contract and refuse all claims`)
#ASSERT r6's `premiums to return` EQUALS 0
-- F1
#ASSERT r6's `may give notice of its rights for the future`
#ASSERT r6's `may terminate by reasonable notice`

r7 MEANS `the insurer's remedy for` consumerK `and` carelessM `given` (`entered with` TRUE 300) `and` (`money` 300 300 0 10000 8000)
-- R7
#ASSERT r7's `amount payable on the claim` EQUALS 8000

r8 MEANS `the insurer's remedy for` consumerK `and` carelessM `given` (`entered with` TRUE 300) `and` (`money` 300 300 0 10000 10000)
-- R8
#ASSERT r8's `amount payable on the claim` EQUALS 10000

§§ `Goal 3 — remedies, paras 7-8 (higher premium)`

r9 MEANS `the insurer's remedy for` consumerK `and` carelessM `given` higher400 `and` baseX
-- R9: X = 75
#ASSERT r9's `amount payable on the claim` EQUALS 7500
#ASSERT NOT (r9's `contract treated as on the different terms`)
#ASSERT NOT (r9's `may avoid the contract and refuse all claims`)
-- F2
#ASSERT r9's `may give notice of its rights for the future`
#ASSERT r9's `may terminate by reasonable notice`

-- R10: X = 50
r10 MEANS `the insurer's remedy for` consumerK `and` carelessM `given` (`entered with` FALSE 1000) `and` (`money` 500 500 0 8000 8000)
#ASSERT r10's `amount payable on the claim` EQUALS 4000

-- R11: X = 33 1/3
r11 MEANS `the insurer's remedy for` consumerK `and` carelessM `given` (`entered with` FALSE 750) `and` (`money` 250 250 0 9000 9000)
#ASSERT r11's `amount payable on the claim` EQUALS 3000

-- R12: X = 99.9
r12 MEANS `the insurer's remedy for` consumerK `and` carelessM `given` (`entered with` FALSE 1000) `and` (`money` 999 999 0 1000 1000)
#ASSERT r12's `amount payable on the claim` EQUALS 999

-- R13: X = 25
r13 MEANS `the insurer's remedy for` consumerK `and` carelessM `given` (`entered with` FALSE 400) `and` (`money` 100 100 0 2000 2000)
#ASSERT r13's `amount payable on the claim` EQUALS 500

-- the para 8 helper directly
#ASSERT `the claim` 10000 `reduced proportionately from` 300 `to` 400 EQUALS 7500
#ASSERT `the claim` 9000 `reduced proportionately from` 250 `to` 750 EQUALS 3000

§§ `Goal 3 — remedies, paras 6 and 7 together`

-- R14: X = 40 of the different-terms claim 6000
r14 MEANS `the insurer's remedy for` consumerK `and` carelessM `given` (`entered with` TRUE 500) `and` (`money` 200 200 0 10000 6000)
#ASSERT r14's `amount payable on the claim` EQUALS 2400
#ASSERT r14's `contract treated as on the different terms`
-- F3
#ASSERT r14's `may give notice of its rights for the future`
#ASSERT r14's `may terminate by reasonable notice`

-- R15
r15 MEANS `the insurer's remedy for` consumerK `and` carelessM `given` (`entered with` TRUE 500) `and` (`money` 200 200 0 10000 0)
#ASSERT r15's `amount payable on the claim` EQUALS 0

-- R16
r16 MEANS `the insurer's remedy for` consumerK `and` carelessM `given` (`entered with` TRUE 600) `and` (`money` 300 300 0 10000 5000)
#ASSERT r16's `amount payable on the claim` EQUALS 2500

§§ `Goal 3 — no qualifying misrepresentation`

-- R17 reasonable care
r17 MEANS `the insurer's remedy for` consumerK `and` carefulM `given` higher400 `and` baseX
#ASSERT r17's `amount payable on the claim` EQUALS 10000
#ASSERT NOT (r17's `may avoid the contract and refuse all claims`)
#ASSERT NOT (r17's `may give notice of its rights for the future`)
#ASSERT NOT (r17's `may terminate by reasonable notice`)

-- R18 same terms, same premium
r18 MEANS `the insurer's remedy for` consumerK `and` carelessM `given` `the same contract on the same terms` `and` baseX
#ASSERT r18's `amount payable on the claim` EQUALS 10000
#ASSERT NOT (r18's `may terminate by reasonable notice`)

-- R17b: a deliberate liar whose lie made no difference has no remedy against him
r17b MEANS `the insurer's remedy for` consumerK `and` deliberateM `given` `the same contract on the same terms` `and` baseX
#ASSERT r17b's `amount payable on the claim` EQUALS 10000
#ASSERT NOT (r17b's `may avoid the contract and refuse all claims`)

§§ `Goal 3 — para 9, life insurance`

-- F4 wholly or mainly life, higher premium: notice yes, terminate no
f4 MEANS `the insurer's remedy for` lifeK `and` carelessM `given` higher400 `and` baseX
#ASSERT f4's `may give notice of its rights for the future`
#ASSERT NOT (f4's `may terminate by reasonable notice`)
#ASSERT f4's `amount payable on the claim` EQUALS 7500

-- F5 life, different terms
f5 MEANS `the insurer's remedy for` lifeK `and` carelessM `given` (`entered with` TRUE 300) `and` (`money` 300 300 0 10000 4000)
#ASSERT f5's `may give notice of its rights for the future`
#ASSERT NOT (f5's `may terminate by reasonable notice`)
#ASSERT f5's `amount payable on the claim` EQUALS 4000

-- life insurance, deliberate or reckless: para 2 still lets the insurer avoid
f5b MEANS `the insurer's remedy for` lifeK `and` deliberateM `given` higher400 `and` baseX
#ASSERT f5b's `may avoid the contract and refuse all claims`

-- life insurance, careless, not on any terms: para 5 avoidance (9(5) only bars 9(4)(b))
f5c MEANS `the insurer's remedy for` lifeK `and` carelessM `given` `no contract on any terms` `and` (`money` 300 900 0 10000 10000)
#ASSERT f5c's `may avoid the contract and refuse all claims`
#ASSERT f5c's `premiums to return` EQUALS 900

§§ `Top-level chain`

GIVEN k IS A `Contract facts`, m IS A `Misrepresentation facts`, w IS A `What the insurer would have done`, x IS A `Money facts`
GIVETH A `Misrepresentation case`
`a case` k m w x MEANS
    `Misrepresentation case` OF k, m, w, x

-- T1
t1 MEANS `the misrepresentation position for` (`a case` consumerK carelessM higher400 baseX)
#ASSERT t1's `the Act applies`
#ASSERT t1's `qualifying misrepresentation` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT t1's `class` EQUALS JUST `careless`
t1r MEANS `the insurer's remedy for` consumerK `and` carelessM `given` higher400 `and` baseX
#ASSERT t1's `remedy` EQUALS JUST t1r
#ASSERT t1r's `amount payable on the claim` EQUALS 7500

-- T2 entered before commencement
t2 MEANS `the misrepresentation position for` (`a case` (`a contract` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE) carelessM higher400 baseX)
#ASSERT NOT (t2's `the Act applies`)
#ASSERT t2's `qualifying misrepresentation` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT t2's `class` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT t2's `remedy` EQUALS NOTHING

-- Q11 company policyholder
q11 MEANS `the misrepresentation position for` (`a case` (`a contract` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE) carelessM `no contract on any terms` baseX)
#ASSERT NOT (q11's `the Act applies`)
#ASSERT q11's `qualifying misrepresentation` EQUALS NOTHING

-- T3 knew untrue, clear question asked, relevance presumed
t3m MEANS `a misrep` TRUE FALSE FALSE (JUST TRUE) FALSE NOTHING FALSE TRUE
t3 MEANS `the misrepresentation position for` (`a case` consumerK t3m higher400 (`money` 300 300 0 10000 10000))
#ASSERT t3's `class` EQUALS JUST `deliberate or reckless`
t3r MEANS `the insurer's remedy for` consumerK `and` t3m `given` higher400 `and` (`money` 300 300 0 10000 10000)
#ASSERT t3r's `may avoid the contract and refuse all claims`
#ASSERT t3r's `amount payable on the claim` EQUALS 0
#ASSERT t3r's `premiums to return` EQUALS 0

-- T4 as T3 with the contrary shown on relevance
t4m MEANS `a misrep` TRUE FALSE FALSE (JUST TRUE) FALSE (JUST FALSE) FALSE TRUE
t4 MEANS `the misrepresentation position for` (`a case` consumerK t4m higher400 baseX)
#ASSERT t4's `class` EQUALS JUST `careless`
t4r MEANS `the insurer's remedy for` consumerK `and` t4m `given` higher400 `and` baseX
#ASSERT t4r's `amount payable on the claim` EQUALS 7500

-- C13 not qualifying: no class
c13 MEANS `the misrepresentation position for` (`a case` consumerK carefulM higher400 baseX)
#ASSERT c13's `qualifying misrepresentation` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT c13's `class` EQUALS NOTHING
